{name:'MycoMap / Mycota Lab',focus:'Community-driven DNA barcoding',description:'Mycota Lab, associated with Stephen Russell, connects documented mushroom collections with DNA sequencing and publicly accessible observation data. The MycoMap network organizes participating geographic projects.',participate:'Check current network locations and submission protocols before collecting or mailing specimens.',url:'https://mycomap.org/projects',link:'Explore MycoMap projects',tag:'DNA & collections'},
{name:'MycoMap BC',focus:'Regional fungal biodiversity in British Columbia',description:'A regional MycoMap effort supported by BC mycological groups and Mycota Lab. It illustrates how local clubs can coordinate documented collections and sequencing.',participate:'Follow the BC project instructions and eligibility requirements; availability can change.',url:'https://mycomap.org/mycomap-bc',link:'Explore MycoMap BC',tag:'Regional collaboration'},
{name:'Mycoquébec',focus:'Regional identification knowledge & reference data',description:'A community-developed resource for Québec fungi, bringing together species accounts, imagery and identification information. It is a model for how regional expertise can become a lasting public resource.',participate:'Compare descriptions, contribute through the community’s established channels, and critically evaluate regional species concepts.',url:'https://www.mycoquebec.org',link:'Explore Mycoquébec',tag:'Identification & education'},
{name:'Fungi Foundation',focus:'Fungal conservation, education & advocacy',description:'Founded by Chilean field mycologist Giuliana Furci, the Fungi Foundation works to bring fungi into conservation policy, public education and biodiversity protection.',participate:'Explore educational materials, campaigns and current ways to support fungal conservation.',url:'https://www.ffungi.org',link:'Explore Fungi Foundation',tag:'Conservation & policy'},
{name:'SPUN',focus:'Mapping underground mycorrhizal diversity',description:'The Society for the Protection of Underground Networks studies and maps mycorrhizal fungi. Its Underground Explorers program supports local researchers and communities with funding, sequencing and protocols.',participate:'Read the Underground Explorers criteria or connect with ongoing local research; grants and participation are not unrestricted.',url:'https://www.spun.earth/get-involved',link:'Explore SPUN opportunities',tag:'Soil ecology'}
];
